.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-04.verdict.txt:39:P2-4. .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/decisions_cli.py:195-202, together with fact_canonical.py:147 and fact_state.py:23/38/54. The new veto_triggered emit, keyed on reason_code, reads only the final decision. When the fact gate in ENFORCE mode, or the ADR-175 citation pilot, replaces a bash_indirect_* block, the new Decision is built without reason_code. Scenario: on those paths no veto_triggered event with the indirect reason code is written; only the fact-gate or citation events are. This affects audit records only; the block decision is unchanged. Minimal fix: pass reason_code=decision.reason_code into the replacement Decision constructors.
