.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-20.verdict.txt:15:4. Moved code: _audit_emit_parts.install (:20-48) and agent_spawn.bind (__init__.py:13-31) rebuild each function with the facade dict as its globals. As a result, monkeypatches on check_agent_spawn, the global writes in _resolve_task_route, and __file__/_HOOKS_DIR lookups behave as before. Default arguments (600 s, 300 s) are still captured at definition time, exactly as before. Mutable state (_FRONTMATTER_MODEL_CACHE) is deep-copied per import. Deep-copying compiled regexes returns the same object on 3.7+. No name collides between the parts or with the names the facade itself defines. Non-__main__ importers (mcp-server/handlers/spawn_agent.py:92, self_test.py:262) still raise on a part import fault rather than allowing.
