.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-27.verdict.txt:23:3. .claude/hooks/_lib/_cost_transcripts_parts/__init__.py:54-56. The class rebuild rebinds every method whose __module__ equals the part's, including the dataclass __repr__ wrapper. functools.wraps / reprlib copy __module__ onto that wrapper, and its body reads a dataclasses/reprlib global (`_thread` or `get_ident`, depending on the Python version). In the facade, repr() or str() of UsageRecord, ScanCounters, Priced and PricingResult therefore raises NameError. No production renderer stringifies them (ceo-cost.py:772 serialises the JSON-safe collect() output), but debugging, logging and test diagnostics break. Fix: rebind only functions whose __code__.co_filename is the part file, or skip __repr__.
